From a87f2a547787eedde696d7ef33779a24d94ef61d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 08:31:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] F5-PROGRESS / HMI-SECOND: F5 never looks dead -- the wait
 page shows the build's progress, and an HMI window left open goes to the wait
 page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20261002: 「又出現 我按F5 編譯沒反應 我把UI 關掉 才編譯的情況」.  Measured (hmi_shell.log, the build dir, oplog): F5 at 08:16:56 opened
the wait page and started the build in the same second; the build ran 6 minutes (390 objects -- cmydef.h had changed with laptop
packages 112-113) while the page said only 「還沒回應」, covering VS Code, so it looked dead and the window was closed at 08:17:40.

* tools/build_with_status.ps1 (new): the same cmake --build (every line passed through for the terminal and the problem matcher,
  cmake's exit code returned), writing web/JSON/runtime/boot_build.js every 0.5 s (percent, objects built, current file, errors).
* .vscode/tasks.json: the three IOWEB builds (ship, -O2, DEBUG) run through it; same build dir, target and -j 6.
* web boot_wait.html (separate commit): reloads that file every second -- 「編譯 NN%（已編 N 個檔）／目前：<file>」, 「編譯完成，程式啟動中」,
  and on a failed build 「編譯失敗」 + the first error line; a status older than the page is ignored; a long build no longer
  triggers the 3-minute warning.
* tools/hmi_shell/hmi_shell.cpp: a second start hands its URL to the running window (WM_COPYDATA) instead of only bringing it to
  the front, so an HMI window left on the old page goes to the wait page F5 asked for.

Verified: the wrapper on build_integ_ship_x86_o2 (up to date, rc 0, state done) and on a missing target (rc 2, state failed);
headless Edge on a copy of boot_wait.html: building / done / failed / stale each shown as above; tasks.json parses (19 tasks);
build_hmi_shell.bat rc 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
